      "description": "Watch Juventus vs NEC highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 17, 2026. The UEFA Europa League group stage kicked off with a highly anticipated clash between Juventus and NEC . Both teams arrived at the stadium under immense pressure to secure their first points of the new European campaign. Early Dominance in Turin On September 17, 2026 , the atmosphere at the stadium was electric as the home side sought to establish early dominance. The breakthrough came just nine minutes in when goalkeeper Kamil Grabara delivered a pinpoint long ball that found Nico Gonzalez , who finished clinically to put Juventus ahead. The momentum stayed firmly with the hosts, and by the 24th minute, Weston McKennie turned provider for Kerim Alajbegovic , who doubled the advantage with a well-taken strike. NEC struggled to contain the waves of pressure, and things went from bad to worse just after the half-hour mark. Following a foul in the area, Nick Woltemade stepped up to the penalty spot in the 35th minute and coolly converted, leaving the visitors with a mountain to climb before the halftime whistle even blew. Tactical Adjustments and Late Goals The second half saw a flurry of tactical changes as both managers looked to freshen up their ranks. Jamiro Monteiro and Douglas Luiz both entered the referee's book as the game became more physical. However, the quality of Juventus eventually shone through again. In the 75th minute, substitute Randal Kolo Muani made an immediate impact by setting up Mehmet Zeki Celik for the fourth goal. Kolo Muani then capped off a brilliant individual performance by scoring himself in the 82nd minute, assisted by Jhon Lucumi , to seal a comprehensive victory. The final whistle confirmed a masterclass from the Italian giants, leaving the fans in high spirits as they celebrated a perfect start to their continental journey."
